// PARAM: --analysis interval
// The sibling of 09 with no dead branch: an unconstrained condition leaves both
// call sites reachable, and they enter f with different values, so the two side
// effects to the shared callee-entry seed key carry two genuinely different
// states rather than bottom and a state.
//
// This is why guarding the callee-entry side effect on a bottom entered state
// -- Goblint's `if not (S.D.is_bot v) then sidel (FunctionEntry f, fc) v` --
// does not by itself settle the shared-resume-node case: whichever of the two
// live writes the solver evaluates first is still a partial accumulate, and the
// per-origin slot still dips when it lands. The contract that does settle it is
// that one right-hand-side evaluation contributes one aggregated value per
// target key.
//
// x is unconstrained, so nothing here claims a value for a -- the check is on
// the caller's own local, which the call cannot touch.
void f(n) {
  return n
}
void main() {
  x := __voblint_nondet_int();
  y := 7;
  if (x < 2) {
    a := f(1)
  } else {
    a := f(2)
  };
  __voblint_check(y == 7) // PROVED
}
